    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d99">

                <pb facs="0141" n="125" sameAs="frus:frus1948v09/pg125"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">816.01/12–2448: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Embassy in El Salvador
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-12-24T13:00:00-05:00">December 24,
                            1948—1 p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>135. Question resumption relations El Salvador involved over-all considerations
                    raised by three revolutions.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d99-f1"/> Therefore while Dept
                    sympathizes with your comments re domestic policies new Sal Govt these not
                    determining factors.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lovett</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d99-f1" n="1" xml:id="d99-f1-content">
                <p>In Peru, El Salvador, and Venezuela.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
